e is never given as 51-59%. Dana is shown as the top author at 1,324, flagged as misleading. The numbers do not meet the criterion.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer B flags Dana's 1,324 lines as misleading and explains that about 1,100 come from a vendored file and about 220 from a reformat. It still lists her at 1,324 and does not give a corrected share. Her naive share would be above 10%, and the table shows her as the largest author. This fails.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer B describes Priya only as 'small' with two commits. It does not credit her with about 28 lines. It does not mention Tomas Ibarra at all.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B does not state a bus factor or any top-two share. It names Hartley and Arnon as the two people to lose, but gives no figures.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B calls Nathaniel Smith unresponsive, with a last commit in 2022. It does not mention Delgan, and it does not report the share of lines owned by departed people.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C ranks Dana Kessler first at 44% and Hartley second at 29%. Arnon is third at 7%, and his identities are not merged in the table. This matches the failure condition.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C presents Dana as the largest owner at 44%. It notes the vendored file and says her share is about 11% without it. That is 10% or more, and she is presented as a major owner in the table. This fails.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C does not credit Priya with her lines. It says only that she is probably active. Tomas Ibarra is not mentioned.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C gives a project-level bus factor of about 2. It does not identify Hartley alone as holding more than half of the lines, and it does not report a top-two share of 63-71%.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C says Arnon has been inactive since 2022, which is wrong. It marks Delgan as unknown and gives no share of lines owned by departed people. This fails.\", \"pass\": false}]}","ttft_ms":12465,"type":"result","duration_ms":12487,"uuid":"015d9c46-3e52-4c36-bdd5-3f5bd24dbe8e","ttft_stream_ms":1892,"time_to_request_ms":431,"first_content_frame_ms":1893,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
